      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Regulatory Compliance: IBA‑Approved Movers, GST Bills &amp; IRCTC Bike Parcel Integration</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;">**Subject: URGENT: Compliance Alert for IBA Mover Operations and IRCTC Integration**

Dear Operations Managers and Fleet Supervisors,

This alert outlines critical compliance requirements for all International Business Association (IBA) approved movers operating within the national logistics network. As we expand our digital footprint through integration with IRCTC’s bike parcel booking system, strict adherence to regulatory frameworks is no longer optional—it is mandatory for operational continuity.

First, ensure that all authorized movers possess a valid IBA mover code. This unique identifier is essential for verifying legitimacy on the platform. Without an active, verified code, your account will be automatically suspended from receiving new bookings. Second, GST invoicing must be generated in real-time for every transaction. The invoice must clearly state the GSTIN, service description, and tax breakdown. Failure to issue a digitally signed GST invoice renders the transaction non-compliant, exposing the company to immediate audit risks.

Third, e-Way bill generation is strictly required for all interstate movements of goods exceeding the prescribed threshold. The e-Way bill must be generated before the vehicle departs the origin point and must remain accessible digitally throughout the journey. Customs and transport authorities may conduct random checks, and the absence of a valid e-Way bill results in immediate vehicle detention.

Crucially, our new service syncs directly with the IRCTC bike parcel booking online portal. When a customer books a bike parcel via the IRCTC app or website, the system automatically assigns the task to an approved mover. The mover must confirm acceptance within 15 minutes. The logistics data, including weight, dimensions, and route details, is pre-populated from the IRCTC booking. Movers must cross-verify this data with physical inspections. Any discrepancy must be reported immediately through the driver app to avoid liability issues.

**⚠️ MANDATORY DOCUMENTS & PENALTIES CALLOUT**

| **Category** | **Details** |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Mandatory Documents** | 1. Valid IBA Mover Code Certificate.<br>2. GST Registration Certificate.<br>3. Digital e-Way Bill (for interstate transport).<br>4. Proof of Insurance for cargo.<br>5. Vehicle Registration and Fitness Certificates. |
| **Penalties for Non-Compliance** | • **GST Error:** 100% of tax amount plus 18% interest per month.<br>• **No e-Way Bill:** 100% of tax amount or ₹5,000 (whichever is lower) plus detention costs.<br>• **IBA Code Lapse:** Immediate permanent ban from the IRCTC platform.<br>• **Data Mismatch:** 20% penalty on service fee and potential legal action. |

Compliance is the backbone of our operational integrity. Ensure all drivers and dispatch staff are briefed on these protocols by end-of-day. Non-compliance jeopardizes our partnership with IRCTC and our legal standing.

